# Reactive UI
@scenario tutorial_lesson_21
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide notes]
pip: A facet displays values from the running game. This example binds a progress bar to a variable.
pip: Open the example below. Then change example_progress in the script and open it again.
> Open the sample panel -> checklist
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label checklist
[set example_name Progress]
[set example_progress 0.75]
[screen call tutorial_card]
@label check
pip: What should drive a progress bar?
> The state value that changes. -> correct
> A copied screenshot of the readout. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: A binding reads the current value whenever the UI updates. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: A binding reads the current value whenever the UI updates.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_21]
[flag tutorial_done_21]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_4]
